WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.004
A caregiver gets home with a discharge sheet and a potassium result still
pending.

2
00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:07.616
Follow-up is due within two days.

3
00:00:07.825 --> 00:00:10.704
But nobody is named to call the family.

4
00:00:11.517 --> 00:00:16.207
Making the document easier to read does not answer who owns that next
step.

5
00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:22.488
Atropos MedPlain brings the original documents and caregiver concern into
one review.

6
00:00:22.999 --> 00:00:28.154
Strands agents index the evidence, connect relevant passages and build a
source-cited

7
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.547
clarification card.

8
00:00:30.151 --> 00:00:32.774
The medication regimen stays unresolved.

9
00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:37.848
The system asks for clarification instead of inventing the missing result
or owner.

10
00:00:38.359 --> 00:00:39.973
Now the question can move.

11
00:00:40.216 --> 00:00:44.756
Assign it to a synthetic staff actor, explicitly select that actor, and

12
00:00:44.802 --> 00:00:46.428
accept the task.

13
00:00:46.869 --> 00:00:49.725
Record an answer tied to the original witnesses.

14
00:00:50.235 --> 00:00:53.672
That answer cannot change the discharge instructions.

15
00:00:53.997 --> 00:00:58.769
Switch to operator to record and submit a separate source revision.

16
00:00:59.373 --> 00:01:04.551
After verification, switch back to reviewer to link it and confirm
closure.

17
00:01:04.992 --> 00:01:07.558
The original evidence remains intact.

18
00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:11.029
Review and release the exact child card.

19
00:01:11.308 --> 00:01:14.013
Its ordinary patient link stays read-only.

20
00:01:14.338 --> 00:01:18.378
A separate response link lets the patient explain the highlighted
information in

21
00:01:18.413 --> 00:01:19.434
their own words.

22
00:01:19.875 --> 00:01:24.473
A bounded Strands assessment proposes what appears missing or
misunderstood.

23
00:01:24.914 --> 00:01:29.546
The reviewer checks that proposal, requests follow-up when needed, and
retains the

24
00:01:29.593 --> 00:01:31.683
next response as a separate attempt.

25
00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:36.094
This is provisional review, not certified understanding.

26
00:01:37.209 --> 00:01:42.212
Targeted retrieval supplies versioned educational passages with exact
citations.

27
00:01:42.723 --> 00:01:46.717
It cannot fill in a patient's missing dose, owner or treatment.

28
00:01:47.228 --> 00:01:50.595
The deterministic safety gate remains strict throughout.

29
00:01:51.036 --> 00:01:52.441
The evidence is mixed.

30
00:01:52.824 --> 00:01:58.652
Prepared examples and release checks are offline fixtures, not new Bedrock
success.

31
00:01:59.163 --> 00:02:04.945
Our completed historical comparison found nine annotated relationships
versus four for the

32
00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.706
full baseline, but delivered only twenty-five of thirty cards.

33
00:02:09.031 --> 00:02:10.587
Five refusals remain.

34
00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:15.800
A later diagnostic stopped after one verified card and one refusal; its

35
00:02:15.858 --> 00:02:17.716
comparison never ran.

36
00:02:18.528 --> 00:02:20.572
Clinical benefit is unmeasured.

37
00:02:20.955 --> 00:02:22.545
Try the anonymous demo.

38
00:02:23.056 --> 00:02:27.398
Trace a question to its sources, follow its accepted next step, and

39
00:02:27.456 --> 00:02:29.209
inspect the complete evidence.
